        {
          "line_number": 6,
          "text": "Use the supplied task image (Godot4.4.1/Python3), from /workspace with this delivered directory at output/.\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 7,
          "text": "The image default user requires writable Godot user-data. Use a writable HOME, for example:\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 8,
          "text": "HOME=/tmp python3 /opt/fx-tools/export_effects.py --project output/project --output output/preview\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 9,
          "text": "From the delivery root, use --project project --output preview with the same writable HOME context.\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 10,
          "text": "For an independent fresh capture, change only the output path to /tmp/reference-repeat. Then compare state records and all decoded image channels:\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 11,
          "text": "python3 output/verification/compare_preview.py --submitted output/preview --fresh /tmp/reference-repeat --output /tmp/preview-correspondence.json\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 12,
          "text": "Different PNG encodings are acceptable when decoded image pixels match. Reproducibility does not by itself establish correctness; independent API and world/timing observations below remain separate.\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 21,
          "text": "## Capture Model\n"
        },
        {
          "line_number": 22,
          "text": "The prescribed exporter samples real headless Godot state and runtime texture pixels, then composes dark/light images with Pillow. These are CPU reconstructions, not GPU framebuffer screenshots. The ordinary MIX/source-texture project uses supported features; arbitrary custom shaders, clipping or occluding/draw-order interventions are outside this preview model. The paired images support their declared state/artwork scope. The independent public-API checks support event/object/timing relations separately. A repeat export demonstrates artifact correspondence; reproducibility alone is not proof of correctness.\n"
        },
